                    {
                        "recommendationid": "73246933",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198023639387",
                            "num_reviews": 21,
                            "playtime_forever": 273,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 260,
                            "last_played": 1598770873
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Little Reaper 💀 is a very polished puzzle action platformer.\nThe 2.5D art style is cute and quirky yet beautiful. The soundtrack is vibrant and ties in well with each location. The plot is simple and the cutscenes could use a few more frames, but the game more then makes up for this with its handcrafted areas. \n\nWhile there are 4 main worlds, many of them are composed of several sub-biomes. For example, the Asphodel Meadows take place across a garden, giant treetops, crypt, and graveyard. Each of these has its own enemies and obstacles and atmosphere. Bosses guard each exit, requiring you to prove your mastery of each new ability.\n\nThe game is quite forgiving, with multiple checkpoints and several hitpoints but is still tricky to master. The puzzles in the first two areas are mostly straightforward but get more challenging as you progress.\n\nI only found one bug, which they fixed within a day of my mention\nThe controls are fluid and precise and as you progress you unlock more movement abilities (such as dashing, scythe teleportation, etc.).\n\nLittle Reaper is definitely a game worth playing through to the end!",
